[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-71983"] :question/problem "Write the complex number $z=-1+\\text{i}$ in exponential form." :question/worked-solution "To write our complex number in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{(1)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the second quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-1)| \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=\\sqrt{2}$ and $\\theta =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get \n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{e}}^{3\\pi \\text{i}/4}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-71982/selection/688e0f503835445066d1de6d51ef8528c067bfad6f88d2cda3908a5b525bcfac" :answer/id #uuid "cb001d66-cfe8-50c4-91eb-eeef3fc4f15c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=2\\,{\\text{e}}^{5\\pi \\text{i}/6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71982/selection/94820436926bea79ec6e3c1d8f7a29e49b2a97de649615501abe5e3940bc7599" :answer/id #uuid "6f5804c3-e57f-5019-9332-247c2bf41770" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=4\\,{\\text{e}}^{5\\pi \\text{i}/6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71982/selection/a4cd93c50a1175e5ea76af6a2a596ec53f3bf9550acfc2c3751560a3f71ab1e5" :answer/id #uuid "40a4fd16-ba49-55d7-a3b1-80c57a741c0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=3\\,{\\text{e}}^{3\\pi \\text{i}/4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71982/selection/caeeaf1f454d52e8e5f16ecc5b13f68961072d4315a8ac75ce5c697727648003" :answer/id #uuid "961e466a-b8cd-5132-841d-14614c537c8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=2\\,{\\text{e}}^{2\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71982/selection/dea5a50bb62b635f144b31b69a78b2a8337aa1f481083940d84e931de872668e" :answer/id #uuid "0e1801c1-82f3-53ef-9c73-e7bb37b211d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=4\\,{\\text{e}}^{2\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71982/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f3f5060a-1c15-5222-8845-c82dc040cd70" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71982/selection/dea5a50bb62b635f144b31b69a78b2a8337aa1f481083940d84e931de872668e" :answer-field/choices ["q-71982/selection/688e0f503835445066d1de6d51ef8528c067bfad6f88d2cda3908a5b525bcfac" "q-71982/selection/94820436926bea79ec6e3c1d8f7a29e49b2a97de649615501abe5e3940bc7599" "q-71982/selection/a4cd93c50a1175e5ea76af6a2a596ec53f3bf9550acfc2c3751560a3f71ab1e5" "q-71982/selection/caeeaf1f454d52e8e5f16ecc5b13f68961072d4315a8ac75ce5c697727648003" "q-71982/selection/dea5a50bb62b635f144b31b69a78b2a8337aa1f481083940d84e931de872668e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71982" :question/id #uuid "1956a1cf-0621-5528-be75-0d024fb52de7" :question/math-academy-id "q-71982" :question/problem "Write the complex number $z=-2+2\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}$ in exponential form." :question/worked-solution "To write our complex number in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{(2\\sqrt{3})}^{2}} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the second quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{2})| \\\\  & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\sqrt{3})| \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=4$ and $\\theta =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get \n\n$$\nz=4\\,{\\text{e}}^{2\\pi \\text{i}/3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-71982/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01caf021-de3e-5e2a-89ce-ba289b65c0ff"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71982"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71977/selection/66f93fb75f5f9d1685a48f650f7f1b24863db6b345fd9ae0628f30c8f80c2e09" :answer/id #uuid "bd6e07f2-a1a8-5c1a-aaf0-4be796cdd52b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=2\\,{\\text{e}}^{7\\pi \\text{i}/6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71977/selection/f0d852b3aef7b9a1b11c05cf6f14e407bf7cf66e330c0511f019b9fab770d0c6" :answer/id #uuid "510f1f24-da71-5fb0-8b1e-55993f709c0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=3\\,{\\text{e}}^{7\\pi \\text{i}/6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71977/selection/0020e9c1807ab454cc86a7bfb12d6b73c0b6d57bc4d1ac0622c0991bad4021cf" :answer/id #uuid "c51b3536-c284-5d28-8adc-ff6837d788bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=2\\,{\\text{e}}^{4\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71977/selection/f4e978c875ea0631efaa0d03265830670926c0246f40d8a88cb0e5ca2c3b403f" :answer/id #uuid "1e6b2906-4026-5c71-828f-542888675ef7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=3\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{e}}^{4\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71977/selection/8b5cfb6b6db9f64b6a3a7a451ea70551ae82a710b375ba50f670362fe5c3787d" :answer/id #uuid "1b0da3ec-a3b7-5fc1-be5b-c509ba4a9f89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=3\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5\\pi \\text{i}/4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71977/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3b33d743-b84e-5a1c-b068-3d2785829e58" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71977/selection/66f93fb75f5f9d1685a48f650f7f1b24863db6b345fd9ae0628f30c8f80c2e09" :answer-field/choices ["q-71977/selection/66f93fb75f5f9d1685a48f650f7f1b24863db6b345fd9ae0628f30c8f80c2e09" "q-71977/selection/f0d852b3aef7b9a1b11c05cf6f14e407bf7cf66e330c0511f019b9fab770d0c6" "q-71977/selection/0020e9c1807ab454cc86a7bfb12d6b73c0b6d57bc4d1ac0622c0991bad4021cf" "q-71977/selection/f4e978c875ea0631efaa0d03265830670926c0246f40d8a88cb0e5ca2c3b403f" "q-71977/selection/8b5cfb6b6db9f64b6a3a7a451ea70551ae82a710b375ba50f670362fe5c3787d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71977" :question/id #uuid "0c35421b-6fda-58ba-a484-a63392e2ff00" :question/math-academy-id "q-71977" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/a02f84856db56412060d6f376f3d926e3fb05581ee36ef9b5e4d2cc570e8438d.png)\n\nWrite the complex number $z$, shown on the Argand diagram above, in exponential form." :question/worked-solution "The complex number shown in the Argand diagram can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =x+\\text{i}y \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{3}-\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo write it in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(-\\sqrt{3})}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the third quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi +|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =\\pi +|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{-1}{-\\sqrt{3}})| \\\\  & =\\pi +|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})| \\\\  & =\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=2$ and $\\theta =\\frac{7\\pi }{6}$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get \n\n$$\nz=2\\,{\\text{e}}^{7\\pi \\text{i}/6}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-71977/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9be02ade-3dd2-5ec3-a532-78d1151dc89f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71977"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-8080/selection/007afe6f80a03532cc4e8fcfd9f57c385564f044afbddab0f3fd7418c5e79917" :answer/id #uuid "e6e31482-f332-5c48-b33b-ae038c3038ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{-3\\pi \\text{i}/4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8080/selection/98ddd28c0ba6ce612b611a02f96ec330b8c1a60251dfcb68992980b763947038" :answer/id #uuid "6e35b692-bf1b-50d4-9ac8-d93861c08ab1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{3\\pi \\text{i}/4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8080/selection/277875c2725afb043a1a6b9b9298f604581ba226a4e9e160dc091fdaa10ee5dc" :answer/id #uuid "2a0d3b65-b551-5e87-8dc6-aa2b512ddf8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=3\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{e}}^{-3\\pi \\text{i}/4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8080/selection/2a5a849c6202d673cdc0342dc5f749c784d1f833f39e05201aa02ca10d9ad67b" :answer/id #uuid "ce12461c-00cb-51db-9f2f-1c7999047139" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=3\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{e}}^{-\\pi \\text{i}/4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8080/selection/1ea87392e4452270653b6c7c6ce5ef7d93b2cbcbea87ae054814067940e2cc9d" :answer/id #uuid "0fd2a0f6-f5f9-5bf5-ad6c-a4c5431ce43d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=3\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{e}}^{3\\pi \\text{i}/4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8080/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "741d8bc4-ef47-54c7-ab7d-7bb95d37c496" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-8080/selection/1ea87392e4452270653b6c7c6ce5ef7d93b2cbcbea87ae054814067940e2cc9d" :answer-field/choices ["q-8080/selection/007afe6f80a03532cc4e8fcfd9f57c385564f044afbddab0f3fd7418c5e79917" "q-8080/selection/98ddd28c0ba6ce612b611a02f96ec330b8c1a60251dfcb68992980b763947038" "q-8080/selection/277875c2725afb043a1a6b9b9298f604581ba226a4e9e160dc091fdaa10ee5dc" "q-8080/selection/2a5a849c6202d673cdc0342dc5f749c784d1f833f39e05201aa02ca10d9ad67b" "q-8080/selection/1ea87392e4452270653b6c7c6ce5ef7d93b2cbcbea87ae054814067940e2cc9d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8080" :question/id #uuid "41f8ed0e-3f5f-5a44-847f-9807b6001d1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-8080" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/6e2a47a4563e404bc09f285af6ffcb098ea16a49f9c45e450a70ef0cb54f6263.png)\n\nWrite the complex number $z$, shown on the Argand diagram above, in exponential form." :question/worked-solution "The complex number shown in the Argand diagram can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =x+\\text{i}y \\\\  & =-3+3\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo write it in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{18} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z$ lies in the second quadrant of the complex plane, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-1)| \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=3\\sqrt{2}$ and $\\theta =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=3\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{e}}^{3\\pi \\text{i}/4}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-8080/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9be02ade-3dd2-5ec3-a532-78d1151dc89f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8080"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-17517"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/d7eb4042a5422d631c867cba1c1fa9c52b400d0061fd5fe7d2fa380d721dbac5.png)\n\nWrite the complex number $z$, shown on the Argand diagram above, in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to three decimal places." :question/worked-solution "The complex number shown in the Argand diagram can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =x+\\text{i}y \\\\  & =4+3\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo write it in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the first quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\  & ≈0.644.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=5$ and $\\theta =0.644$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get \n\n$$\nz=5\\,{\\text{e}}^{0.644\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-107428"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/ba77669a8e0ffd3e69bfc8e5322d7042c318a55b4cd486ac1fac591d3b016e43.png)\n\nWrite the complex number $z$, shown on the Argand diagram above, in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to the nearest tenth." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-71978"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/c5d36b72e7e2ff6754152a559d64bf3610708c9a2d3790c859bc9abacc9220b6.png)\n\nWrite the complex number $z$, shown on the Argand diagram above, in exponential form." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5282"] :question/worked-solution "To write our complex number in the form $z = r\\textrm{e}^{\\textrm{i}\\theta},$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta = \\arg(z),$ we first calculate $r\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z$ lies in the first quadrant of the complex plane, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=4\\sqrt{2}$ and $\\theta=\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$ into $z=re^{\\textrm{i}\\theta},$ we get\n\n$$\nz = 4\\sqrt{2}\\,\\textrm{e}^{\\pi\\textrm{i}/4}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5280"] :question/problem "Write the complex number ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/c93c5bf19eefeb4da980b81d46c4df10b3ff10aca21937aed885ef4111b1c9a7.png), shown in the following Argand diagram, in exponential form.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/335311049419928acc946721242c6e8e4096313dca1290b89b1cc7a2c30748fd.png)" :question/worked-solution "The complex number shown in the Argand diagram can be written as\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/5d6456ae3c5f168a14e761b44085defd76cd2292e8fa8d9b0eedf2cb55d97563.png)\n\nTo write it in the form ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/0eb9bfc5066fce3fe0434f4dedf05cea2fff1e2fe38b32d4223eaf177ca2b654.png) where ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/d3e8106a9b65dceed9a9c4e6fbc6341c0268517854b72f6e34fc3ec80117b915.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/6017ce5c562b2c1a2d1a47371c54820b04852fb851056aa171f88c411d92bd45.png) we first calculate ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/e3862c77b505ea48e95acf4d632fa692c866c65079a2ac6b17543fd54e1c20ca.png)\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/d0bd5d7fc7f1d7b487fd940af95b5abb7e2fb134c02a55dbf9eb7d191abccca8.png)\n\nNow, since ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/c93c5bf19eefeb4da980b81d46c4df10b3ff10aca21937aed885ef4111b1c9a7.png) lies in the second quadrant, we can find the angle ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/f49e0503f6588c93dd1fd274c63f60c06b0eb77d5dce2d12dba750107139f124.png) as\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/96e40550e19a81ffb655cd359242d8b0a37b1dde12e442252f976397a09a9760.png)\n\nto three decimal places.\n\nFinally, substituting ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/5dcf5f8d9a0eb6d36f76152105bcb5a9af61a34bc99719183df2044d7f113edb.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/11dd78699cf02b8b10f1bd6dc78ee987d26954fc8b51a2e8327c2f24b5552458.png) into ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/9ea3d5e030449e3b1da133b0aa004c6d26702021bf66e5672abe2bdd2c69eb9b.png) we get \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077408/assets/dd0d831b250bbf985783cbb745a23c709a481ba08018395c683c3e2d4b00284a.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
